{
  "$schema": "https://etalii.net/adp/fbl/schema/0.1/fbl.schema.json#/$defs/Fixture",
  "doc": "An insert writes its rule's constants (FBL 0.8, section 6.2), in the json family. The body holds a task and a note in one list, told apart by type. An add of a task writes type: task second, as keys names it; its undo and redo; an add of a note writes its three constants after its keys; a set leaves a constant as it is. ../insert-constant-json-read/ reads the body the last step leaves, and ../insert-constant-yaml/ is the same in the yaml family.",
  "binding": "board.fbl#board",
  "input": "board.json",
  "read": {
    "elements": [
      {
        "id": "t1",
        "type": "Task",
        "attributes": {
          "name": "Plan"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "n1",
        "type": "Note",
        "attributes": {
          "text": "Remember",
          "format": "1.0"
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "steps": [
    {
      "doc": "A task's constant, type: task, is named by keys, so it is written second, after the id and before the name; nothing in the add gives it (FBL 0.8, section 6.2).",
      "edit": {
        "add": {
          "type": "Task",
          "id": "t2",
          "attributes": {
            "name": "Ship"
          }
        }
      },
      "splices": [
        {
          "operation": "insert-entry",
          "start": 227,
          "end": 227,
          "text": ",\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"t2\",\r\n      \"type\": \"task\",\r\n      \"name\": \"Ship\"\r\n    }"
        }
      ],
      "expect": "{\r\n  \"elements\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"t1\",\r\n      \"type\": \"task\",\r\n      \"name\": \"Plan\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"n1\",\r\n      \"text\": \"Remember\",\r\n      \"type\": \"note\",\r\n      \"format\": \"1.0\",\r\n      \"pinned\": false\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"t2\",\r\n      \"type\": \"task\",\r\n      \"name\": \"Ship\"\r\n    }\r\n  ]\r\n}\r\n"
    },
    {
      "doc": "The undo removes the new entry, its constant with it; it is listed under the operation of the splice it inverts (section 15.3).",
      "undo": true,
      "splices": [
        {
          "operation": "insert-entry",
          "start": 227,
          "end": 306,
          "text": ""
        }
      ],
      "expect": "{\r\n  \"elements\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"t1\",\r\n      \"type\": \"task\",\r\n      \"name\": \"Plan\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"n1\",\r\n      \"text\": \"Remember\",\r\n      \"type\": \"note\",\r\n      \"format\": \"1.0\",\r\n      \"pinned\": false\r\n    }\r\n  ]\r\n}\r\n"
    },
    {
      "doc": "The redo writes the same bytes again.",
      "redo": true,
      "splices": [
        {
          "operation": "insert-entry",
          "start": 227,
          "end": 227,
          "text": ",\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"t2\",\r\n      \"type\": \"task\",\r\n      \"name\": \"Ship\"\r\n    }"
        }
      ],
      "expect": "{\r\n  \"elements\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"t1\",\r\n      \"type\": \"task\",\r\n      \"name\": \"Plan\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"n1\",\r\n      \"text\": \"Remember\",\r\n      \"type\": \"note\",\r\n      \"format\": \"1.0\",\r\n      \"pinned\": false\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"t2\",\r\n      \"type\": \"task\",\r\n      \"name\": \"Ship\"\r\n    }\r\n  ]\r\n}\r\n"
    },
    {
      "doc": "A note's constants are not named by keys, so they follow its keys in the order the constant lists them: type, format, pinned. format is the string 1.0, which is not plain-safe, so it is written in the binding's quote and reads back as the same text; pinned is the bool false, written as such. The text yes is not plain-safe either (section 6.3).",
      "edit": {
        "add": {
          "type": "Note",
          "id": "n2",
          "attributes": {
            "text": "yes"
          }
        }
      },
      "splices": [
        {
          "operation": "insert-entry",
          "start": 306,
          "end": 306,
          "text": ",\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"n2\",\r\n      \"text\": \"yes\",\r\n      \"type\": \"note\",\r\n      \"format\": \"1.0\",\r\n      \"pinned\": false\r\n    }"
        }
      ],
      "expect": "{\r\n  \"elements\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"t1\",\r\n      \"type\": \"task\",\r\n      \"name\": \"Plan\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"n1\",\r\n      \"text\": \"Remember\",\r\n      \"type\": \"note\",\r\n      \"format\": \"1.0\",\r\n      \"pinned\": false\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"t2\",\r\n      \"type\": \"task\",\r\n      \"name\": \"Ship\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"n2\",\r\n      \"text\": \"yes\",\r\n      \"type\": \"note\",\r\n      \"format\": \"1.0\",\r\n      \"pinned\": false\r\n    }\r\n  ]\r\n}\r\n"
    },
    {
      "doc": "A set of the new task's name replaces that value only; the constant's bytes stay as they are (section 6.4).",
      "edit": {
        "set": {
          "element": "t2",
          "attributes": {
            "name": "Ship it"
          }
        }
      },
      "splices": [
        {
          "operation": "replace-value",
          "start": 293,
          "end": 299,
          "text": "\"Ship it\""
        }
      ],
      "expect": "{\r\n  \"elements\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"t1\",\r\n      \"type\": \"task\",\r\n      \"name\": \"Plan\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"n1\",\r\n      \"text\": \"Remember\",\r\n      \"type\": \"note\",\r\n      \"format\": \"1.0\",\r\n      \"pinned\": false\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"t2\",\r\n      \"type\": \"task\",\r\n      \"name\": \"Ship it\"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"n2\",\r\n      \"text\": \"yes\",\r\n      \"type\": \"note\",\r\n      \"format\": \"1.0\",\r\n      \"pinned\": false\r\n    }\r\n  ]\r\n}\r\n"
    }
  ]
}
